§P root.cause
  ✓ MIR record constructor previously emitted opaque `cssl.struct`.
  ✓ Cranelift.object allocated every multi-field record as N×8-byte stack storage.
  ✓ `cssl.field` forwarded aggregate address instead of extracting field value.
  ✓ signature resolver independently scalarized ≤8-byte nominal records.
  ∴ function-boundary carrier and body construction/projection disagreed ; profile
    observed address-like projection instead of `{tag:u32,value:u32}` bits.

§D accepted.delta
  1. MirStructLayout retains exact declaration field names + natural byte offsets
     + size/alignment ; duplicate bare identities become pathless sentinels.
  2. production csslc root+aux lowering supplies one exact struct-layout table to
     ordinary + direct-call body lowering ; legacy no-table MIR API remains intact.
  3. admission requires named+unique+declaration-backed fields ; field types belong
     to {bool,i8,u8,i16,u16,i32,u32,i64,u64} ; recomputed natural layout matches.
  4. admitted total byte size ∈ {1,2,4,8} ; carrier width ∈ {8,16,32,64}.
  5. constructor source order canonicalizes to declaration order ; shorthand fields
     resolve exact bindings ; MIR records names+offsets+widths+carrier+little-endian.
  6. projection resolves declaration field and emits typed shift+reduce metadata.
  7. Cranelift.object+JIT pack fields by zero-extension+shift+OR and project by
     logical shift+reduction ; malformed metadata fails before object/JIT execution.
  8. private compiler-managed param+return uses exact scalar carrier identity.
  9. Windows.x64 public C import/export admits only exact natural aggregate sizes
     1|2|4|8 ; profile `{u32,u32}` raw by-value parameter+return verified.
  10. profile ABI9001 status changes 9001→0 without widening ABI9002..ABI9005.

§D refusal.contract
  typed.MIR := `cssl.nominal_record.error` {code,detail,source_loc}.
  codes := {
    ABI9001-UNRESOLVED-PATH, ABI9001-MISSING-LAYOUT,
    ABI9001-PATHLESS-LAYOUT, ABI9001-UNSUPPORTED-LAYOUT,
    ABI9001-FIELD-SET-MISMATCH, ABI9001-DUPLICATE-FIELD,
    ABI9001-FIELD-TYPE-MISMATCH, ABI9001-UNSUPPORTED-FIELD,
    ABI9001-UNKNOWN-FIELD, ABI9001-MALFORMED-METADATA,
    ABI9001-WINDOWS-C-UNSUPPORTED-LAYOUT
  }.
  refused.layout := {empty,tuple|pathless,duplicate-name,unresolved,
    float,pointer,nested-record,nonnatural-offset,size3|5|6|7|>8}.
  ✓ legacy.native-x64 signature refusal remains `X64-0001` + no object.
  ✓ legacy.native-x64 nominal-op refusal remains `X64-0015` + no object.
  ✓ legacy private/pathless direct-MIR signature behavior remains unchanged unless
    exact ABI9001 production layout-aware path or public Windows-C validator applies.

